Overall, a winning strategy.  Most of what I have to say has been said
by others already, so I'll just add that in your responses below, you
still seem to be concerned a bit too much on optimizing what you'll
eventually have. Just *survive* to the Castle.  The castle wand will
give you anything you want except maybe artifacts, and as long as
you've got *some* good artifact weapon (like Mojo), most of the things
you need aren't artifacts.  And the valk also gets the Orb of Fate
guaranteed, which is one of the best quest artifacts (half-physical
damage *and* half-spell damage *and* levelport).  Sure, if you get
both the Orb and the Eye, you'll have so much mobility that stairs
will seem archaic, but a suboptimal set of gear *now* will help more
than the best possible gear 10 levels after you died.

Also, note that you can make new unholy water the same as with holy
water, and it's even more useful to do so since you can get holy water
through prayer without annoying your god.  No so much with unholy
water, so if you find some, be sure to #dip a few more before you use
the first one.


